{
  "borough": "Hounslow",
  "application_type": "All Other",
  "decision": "Refused",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "Reason : 1 - The proposal would be out of scale and not in keeping with the character and scale of the prevailing built form. The excessive height of the proposal would result in a domineering overdevelopment in this prominent corner location that would result in harm to the character and appearance of the local area and streetscene. The proposal would be unacceptable in design terms contrary to Local Plan policies CC1 and CC2",
    "Reason : 2 - Due to the excessive height of the proposal coupled with the projection beyond the rear of 2 Exeter Road the proposal would result in a loss of outlook and a sense of enclosure for the neighbours. The proposal would result in unacceptable harm to the living conditions of neighbours contrary to Local Plan policies CC1 and CC2.",
    "Reason : 3 - Without satisfactory evidence to the contrary the proposal has not demonstrated that there would not be an unacceptable increase in parking stress within the local area, to the detriment of highway and pedestrian safety and contrary to London Plan T4 and Local Plan policy EC2",
    "Reason : 4 - Without evidence to the contrary the proposal would fail to achieve an acceptable Biodiversity Net Gain contrary to London Plan policies G6 and G7 and Local Plan policy BG7."
  ],
